{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Voices Of Angels feels like a strong next choice because its vocal and orchestral sound connects with what I enjoyed in Under One Sky and Lead With Your Heart.",
    "Hamilton connects with my interest in Stages and A Musical Affair, while Blown Away connects with my listening to 747 and Golden; these feel like specific, meaningful connections."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Christmas albums connect with earlier listening, but I do not want seasonal music right now, even when the vocal harmonies appeal to me.",
    "Nightbird and Something Beautiful do not give me enough familiar musical context to choose them over clearer matches; I am uncertain about their fit rather than opposed to them."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My earlier Christmas listening seems to have been treated as an ongoing preference regardless of my current mood.",
    "An appeal to expressive singing alone does not make every vocal album equally compelling; 25 interests me, but other choices connect more directly with my listening."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My most recent relaxing classical listening deserves more attention, particularly when choosing between seasonal music and soothing vocal or orchestral music.",
    "I choose selectively: Riser fits my country interest, but I would try Blown Away first, so a plausible connection does not always mean I would choose an album now."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my theatrical, vocal and country interests, but give too much weight to past Christmas listening and too little to my current relaxing mood and selective choices."
}"}
